;
BASIC COMMANDS

DIR or SDZ lists files. Examples: DIR P:   DIR HELP:   DIR J1:
LT reads text. Example: LT A0:WELCOME.TXT
HELP topic displays instructions. Example: HELP MOUNT
MOUNT /L lists the swappable volumes; MOUNT GAMES selects GAMES.
RBBS enters the bulletin board. BYE ends your call.

A0:SYSTEM contains caller commands. I0:WORK is temporary workspace.
I14:HELP contains these topics. J: is the selected swappable volume.
P0:SIGM and P1:CPMUG contain the permanent archive collections.
Use a DU prefix such as J1: to specify drive J, user area 1.
Caller access is controlled by the sysop. A visible program is not
necessarily approved for online execution.
